-- Source module: Solutions.KFGPair
/-!
# KFG: a pointwise `2 × 2` scaled operation on two arbitrary role streams

On the data stack `pre ++ u ++ gap ++ v ++ rest` (Gaussian streams, `|u| = |v| = L`),
`pairP M` replaces `(u, v)` by `(M₀₀ u + M₀₁ v, M₁₀ u + M₁₁ v)` entrywise, with scaled
coefficients `c · 2^d`.  The prefix and the gap are parked on `qP`, `qQ`; the two streams are
distributed to the four register stacks and zipped (`zipRS`); the outputs are moved back.  Every
entry is touched `O(1)` times; the loop counters are unary (`fcode`).

* `pairP_fsp`: the program with its counts in registers (`rB = L`, `rB2 = 2L`, `rP = 2|pre|`,
  `rQ = 2|gap|`).
* `pairW M L i j`: the self-contained wrapper on roles `i < j` of a role-major array with role
  length `L` (`pairW_fsp`, list semantics `pairL`, `getD_pairL`).
-/

